Day 64 - IAM Groups Investigation
Objective
Understand how IAM Groups manage permissions for multiple users.

Investigation
Created an IAM Group
Attached an S3 policy to the group
Added a user to the group
Verified access inheritance
Findings
The user received permissions through the IAM Group.

When the user was removed from the group, access was lost.

Root Cause
Permissions were inherited from the IAM Group.

Resolution
Added the user back to the group and verified access.

Key Takeaway
IAM Groups simplify permission management by assigning policies to groups instead of individual users.
